WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.134
Output encoding represents data so a
particular parser treats it as data rather than

2
00:00:05.214 --> 00:00:06.128
control syntax.

3
00:00:06.208 --> 00:00:10.320
The phrase output encoding is incomplete
unless it names the destination.

4
00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:14.055
HTML text, an HTML attribute, a URL
component, JavaScript source,

5
00:00:14.135 --> 00:00:16.289
and CSS source use different grammars.

6
00:00:16.369 --> 00:00:21.003
A generic helper named escape or
sanitizeString hides the decision developers most

7
00:00:21.083 --> 00:00:21.932
need to review.

8
00:00:22.012 --> 00:00:24.884
In an HTML text position between ordinary
elements,

9
00:00:24.964 --> 00:00:28.097
server templates should use their normal
autoescaping,

10
00:00:28.177 --> 00:00:32.289
or a context-appropriate HTML encoder when
manual output is unavoidable.

11
00:00:32.369 --> 00:00:36.938
Attribute values should be quoted and
serialized through a template or DOM API that

12
00:00:37.018 --> 00:00:38.454
understands attributes.

13
00:00:38.534 --> 00:00:42.385
The attribute name must remain
developer-controlled and innocuous.

14
00:00:42.465 --> 00:00:46.838
Correct attribute serialization prevents a
value from breaking the syntactic

15
00:00:46.918 --> 00:00:50.247
boundary, but it does not make every
attribute meaning safe.

16
00:00:50.327 --> 00:00:54.635
For URLs, construct components with URL
and URLSearchParams or an equivalent

17
00:00:54.715 --> 00:00:55.563
URL-aware API.

18
00:00:55.643 --> 00:00:58.776
Percent encoding preserves data within a
URL component;

19
00:00:58.856 --> 00:01:01.793
it is not HTML encoding, destination
authorization,

20
00:01:01.873 --> 00:01:03.701
or a license to accept any scheme.

21
00:01:03.781 --> 00:01:07.567
When a generated URL is emitted into HTML
source, both layers matter:

22
00:01:07.647 --> 00:01:10.192
the URL must be constructed under a URL
policy,

23
00:01:10.272 --> 00:01:14.450
then placed through an HTML or DOM
mechanism appropriate to that attribute.

24
00:01:14.530 --> 00:01:19.164
Avoid putting untrusted values directly
into executable JavaScript or CSS source.

25
00:01:19.244 --> 00:01:23.617
Prefer JSON responses, framework state
transfer designed for HTML embedding,

26
00:01:23.697 --> 00:01:26.961
or runtime data binding that never creates
a script string.

27
00:01:27.041 --> 00:01:31.675
For dynamic presentation, assign a
specific style property and allowlist the value

28
00:01:31.755 --> 00:01:34.692
vocabulary rather than assemble arbitrary
CSS text.

29
00:01:34.772 --> 00:01:38.166
JavaScript encoding and CSS encoding are
specialized tools,

30
00:01:38.246 --> 00:01:41.575
not reasons to generate broad source from
external strings.

31
00:01:41.655 --> 00:01:44.788
HTML encoding is correct for defined HTML
data contexts.

32
00:01:44.868 --> 00:01:48.980
It is not a universal transform for every
language a browser can interpret.
